        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4049617e-7ccf-54ca-be64-7f5b96a030ee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pago Pago International Airport, Hoonah Airport, Tafuna, Pago Pago, Hoonah, Tutuila, American Samoa, Alaska, Nu'uuli\n- Organizations: United States\n- Topics: airport identifiers, airport locations, licensing\n\nFacts:\n- Pago Pago International Airport has the identifiers IATA PPG, ICAO NSTU, and FAA LID PPG.\n- Pago Pago International Airport is also known as Tafuna Airport.\n- Pago Pago International Airport is a public airport located 7 miles southwest of the central business district of Pago Pago in Tafuna on Tutuila in American Samoa.\n- American Samoa is an unincorporated territory of the United States.\n- Hoonah Airport has the identifiers IATA HNH, ICAO PAOH, and FAA LID HNH.\n- Hoonah Airport is a state-owned public-use airport located 1 nautical mile southeast of the central business district of Hoonah, Alaska.\n- Tafuna is located on a peninsula 1 mile north of Pago Pago International Airport and 1 mile south of Nu'uuli in American Samoa.\n- KJAL was licensed to Tafuna, American Samoa, and served the American Samoa area.",
